ed test.\n\nLine 190 set_options \u2014 covered (stubbed call). Line 192-194 covered.\n\nI think we're complete. Let me also consider adding a test where open_url succeeds for first term and raises for second \u2014 verifies error propagates mid-loop. Optional; adds branch coverage for the loop with exception. I'll skip to keep it tight \u2014 actually, it's cheap and verifies real behavior (partial results are discarded since the exception propagates). Let me add it:\n\n```python\ndef test_run_error_on_second_term_aborts(make_lookup, monkeypatch):\n    lookup = make_lookup()\n    responses = {'http://good.example.com/': FakeResponse(b'ok')}\n\n    def handler(term, **kwargs):\n        response = responses.get(term)\n        if response is None:\n            raise URLError('nope')\n        return response\n\n    _patch_open_url(monkeypatch, handler)\n\n    with pytest.raises(AnsibleError) as excinfo:\n        lookup.run(['http://good.example.com/', 'http://bad.example.com/'])\n\n    assert 'Failed lookup url for http://bad.example.com/' in excinfo.value.message\n```\n\nGood.\n\nNow, module-level docstring? Keep minimal. The user said \"Respond ONLY with the Python code enclosed in backticks\". So just the code block.\n\nLet me also double check the FakeResponse read counting \u2014 I had read_count but don't assert it; drop it to keep clean, or keep simple read. Keep simple.\n\nOne more check on the kwargs equality assertion: the plugin passes `headers=self.get_option('headers')` \u2192 my options dict has `{'X-Test': '1'}` \u2014 same object passed through; equality holds.\n\n`timeout=10` \u2014 int. Fine.\n\nAlso note: `use_gssapi=False`, `unix_socket=None`, `ca_path=None`, `unredirected_headers=[]`.\n\nFinal check on `test_run_forwards_variables_and_kwargs_to_set_options`: `lookup.run(['...'], variables={'k': 'v'}, custom=42)` \u2014 run signature `(self, terms, variables=None, **kwargs)` \u2192 variables={'k':'v'}, kwargs={'custom': 42}. The recording set_option